      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you meant kernel normal tracepoint because there is Vendor Hook only in the aosp kernel.\n\nAs for as I know, typically the purpose of the tracepoint is to trace events using /sys/kernel/debug/tracing and etc.\nEven if a trace event is generated, any user tasks cannot take a chance to perform because these codes will fall directly into die() or panic().\n\n  do_undefinstr()\n    -\u003e BUG()\n      ...\n      -\u003e bug_handler\n        -\u003e die()\n \n  bad_mode()\n    -\u003e panic()\n \n  arm64_serror_panic()\n    -\u003e nmi_panic()\n      -\u003e panic()\n\nThus, these locations are not suitable for general traces and are not very helpful to everyone.\n\nTherefore, I think it is better to insert restricted vendor hooks than to submit normal tracepoints upstream.",
